---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../components/SectionLabel.astro';
import StatBlock from '../components/StatBlock.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="EU AI Act Compliance & AI Governance — OOPUO"
  description="Compliance audits, risk assessments, agent observability, and technical documentation. Avoid fines up to €35M with proper AI governance."
>
  <!-- HERO (dark) -->
  <section data-theme="dark" class="bg-bg-dark py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="max-w-[var(--max-width-site)] mx-auto px-6">
      <SectionLabel class="mb-4 block">For regulated companies</SectionLabel>
      <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-hero text-text-on-dark max-w-4xl mb-6">
        Your AI is powerful. Make sure it's also legal.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-text-on-dark-secondary text-body-lg max-w-[720px] mb-10 leading-relaxed">
        EU AI Act compliance, risk assessments, and technical governance — from an engineering team that understands both your systems and the regulation.
      </p>
      <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Request a Compliance Assessment &rarr;</Button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE STAKES (dark) -->
  <section data-theme="dark" class="bg-bg-dark py-section">
    <div class="max-w-[var(--max-width-site)] mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-h2 text-text-on-dark mb-8 max-w-3xl">
        The EU AI Act isn't coming. It's here.
      </h2>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-12 mb-12">
        <StatBlock value="€35M" label="Maximum fine for prohibited AI practices" />
        <StatBlock value="7%" label="Of global annual turnover for serious violations" />
        <StatBlock value="Art. 6–49" label="Obligations for high-risk AI system deployers" />
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-[720px] space-y-6">
        <p class="text-text-on-dark-secondary text-body-lg leading-relaxed">
          The regulation entered into force in August 2024. Prohibitions on unacceptable AI practices apply from February 2025. High-risk system requirements hit in August 2026. The compliance clock is already running.
        </p>
        <p class="text-text-on-dark-secondary text-body-lg leading-relaxed">
          If your company uses AI for hiring, credit scoring, content moderation, customer profiling, or automated decision-making — you're almost certainly in scope. Even off-the-shelf AI tools can trigger deployer obligations under the Act.
        </p>
        <p class="text-text-on-dark-secondary text-body-lg leading-relaxed">
          The question isn't whether you need to comply. It's whether you'll do it proactively or under enforcement pressure.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SERVICES (light) -->
  <section class="bg-bg-primary py-section">
    <div class="max-w-[var(--max-width-site)] mx-auto px-6">
      <SectionLabel class="mb-8 block">How we help</SectionLabel>

      <div class="space-y-6">
        <!-- Service 1 -->
        <div class="bg-bg-elevated border border-border-subtle shadow-card rounded-[10px] p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-h3 mb-4">Compliance Audit & Gap Analysis</h3>
          <p class="text-text-secondary text-body-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
            We map every AI system in your organization against EU AI Act requirements. You get a clear picture of your risk exposure, obligation category (provider, deployer, distributor), and a prioritized remediation roadmap.
          </p>
          <p class="font-mono text-caption text-accent">
            Deliverable: Comprehensive audit report with risk classification, gap analysis, and actionable compliance timeline.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Service 2 -->
        <div class="bg-bg-elevated border border-border-subtle shadow-card rounded-[10px] p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-h3 mb-4">Risk Assessment & Mitigation</h3>
          <p class="text-text-secondary text-body-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For each AI system classified as high-risk, we conduct a structured risk assessment following the regulation's framework. We identify failure modes, bias vectors, and data governance gaps — then build the controls that close them.
          </p>
          <p class="font-mono text-caption text-accent">
            Deliverable: Per-system risk assessment documentation, mitigation strategies, and residual risk evaluation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Service 3 -->
        <div class="bg-bg-elevated border border-border-subtle shadow-card rounded-[10px] p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-h3 mb-4">Agent Observability & Tracing</h3>
          <p class="text-text-secondary text-body-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
            You can't govern what you can't see. We implement tracing, logging, and monitoring across your AI agents so every decision is recorded, explainable, and auditable. When the regulator asks "why did your system make this decision?" — you have the answer.
          </p>
          <p class="font-mono text-caption text-accent">
            Deliverable: Observability infrastructure deployed, with dashboards, alerting, and audit-ready log exports.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Service 4 -->
        <div class="bg-bg-elevated border border-border-subtle shadow-card rounded-[10px] p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-h3 mb-4">Technical Documentation & Reporting</h3>
          <p class="text-text-secondary text-body-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The EU AI Act requires extensive documentation: data governance records, system architecture descriptions, performance metrics, and human oversight protocols. We write the documentation that satisfies Article 11 requirements — accurate, structured, and maintainable.
          </p>
          <p class="font-mono text-caption text-accent">
            Deliverable: Complete technical documentation package aligned to Annex IV requirements, ready for regulatory review.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OUR APPROACH (light) -->
  <section class="bg-bg-elevated py-section">
    <div class="max-w-[var(--max-width-site)] mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-h2 mb-6">
        Compliance as engineering, not paperwork.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-text-secondary text-body-lg max-w-[720px] mb-12 leading-relaxed">
        Most compliance firms hand you a checklist and a slide deck. We embed with your engineering team. We read the code, understand the architecture, and build compliance into the system — not around it.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-bg-primary border border-border-subtle rounded-[10px] p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-h3 mb-4">Technical depth over surface audits</h3>
          <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            We don't just ask "do you have documentation?" We verify that the documentation matches the system. Architecture reviews, data flow tracing, model evaluation — the work that actually reduces risk.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bg-primary border border-border-subtle rounded-[10px] p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-h3 mb-4">On-premise when privacy demands it</h3>
          <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            Some data can't leave the building. We deploy observability and governance tooling on your infrastructure — local, private cloud, or air-gapped if needed.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bg-primary border border-border-subtle rounded-[10px] p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-h3 mb-4">Sustainable compliance</h3>
          <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            We build processes your team can maintain after we leave. No vendor lock-in, no proprietary platforms, no dependency on us for ongoing operation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TIMELINE (light) -->
  <section class="bg-bg-primary py-section">
    <div class="max-w-[var(--max-width-site)] mx-auto px-6">
      <SectionLabel class="mb-8 block">Typical engagement</SectionLabel>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4 gap-8">
        <div>
          <div class="font-mono text-caption text-accent mb-2">Week 1&ndash;2</div>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-h3 mb-2">Discovery & system inventory</h3>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="font-mono text-caption text-accent mb-2">Week 3&ndash;4</div>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-h3 mb-2">Deep assessment</h3>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="font-mono text-caption text-accent mb-2">Week 5&ndash;8</div>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-h3 mb-2">Implementation & documentation</h3>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="font-mono text-caption text-accent mb-2">Week 9&ndash;10</div>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-h3 mb-2">Review & handoff</h3>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-text-muted text-caption mt-8 italic">
        Timelines vary by scope. A focused engagement on a single AI system can complete in 2&ndash;3 weeks.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FINAL CTA (dark) -->
  <section data-theme="dark" class="bg-bg-dark py-section text-center">
    <div class="max-w-[var(--max-width-site)] mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-h2 text-text-on-dark mb-10">
        Don't wait for the audit to find the gaps.
      </h2>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center items-center">
        <Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Request a Compliance Assessment</Button>
        <a href="mailto:hello@oopuo.com" class="text-text-on-dark-secondary hover:text-text-on-dark transition-colors duration-150">
          Or send us your questions directly &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
